      "argument": [
        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Fix arbitrary F0,n0,U0,G0,W0 as declared. Assume L1: n0>0, U0 is finite-dimensional over F0 with dimension n0, for all a0,b0,c0,d0∈Fin(n0), G0_{a0,b0} G0_{c0,d0}=G0_{a0,d0} when b0=c0 and zero otherwise, ∑_i G0_ii=Id_U0, and W0 is invariant under the entire G0 family. If W0=0, the required zero-or-whole alternative already holds. In the other branch assume L2: W0≠0. Then there exists w∈W0 with w≠0, since otherwise every member would be zero and W0 would be the zero subspace.",
