        },
        {
          "id": "S003",
          "text": "Choose j from F002, and put u=G0_jj w. Invariance gives u∈W0, and u≠0. The multiplication law gives G0_jj u=u by idempotence. Define uvec_i=G0_ij u for every i∈Fin(n0); all uvec_i belong to W0. To prove independence fix arbitrary coefficients coef and assume L3: ∑_i coef_i uvec_i=0. For arbitrary k∈Fin(n0), apply G0_jk. Its product with G0_ij is zero when k≠i, and is G0_jj when k=i. Thus G0_jk uvec_i=0 for i≠k, while G0_jk uvec_k=G0_jj u=u. Linearity reduces the relation to coef_k u=0. Since u≠0 over the field F0, coef_k=0: if nonzero, multiplication by its inverse would force u=0. Every coefficient vanishes. Discharge L3; this proves that uvec is linearly independent.",
          "uses": [],
