        {
          "id": "S004",
          "text": "Apply M002 to Fb=F0,Vb=U0,Jb=Fin(n0),zb=uvec. F003 gives independence; L1 gives finite-dimensionality and |Fin(n0)|=n0=dim_F0 U0. The family spans U0. Since W0 contains its members by F003 and is a subspace, W0 contains their span, hence W0=U0 in the L2 branch. Discharge L2 by combining this branch with the already settled W0=0 branch; the dichotomy holds under L1. Discharge L1 into the quantified implication, and universally quantify the arbitrary data. This proves the claimed universal dichotomy, for any field, without an algebraic-closure condition.",
